panvk: support Valhall v9 (Mali-G57/G68/G77/G78) behind the Job Manager

Upstream PanVK builds the Job Manager backend for Bifrost (v6, v7) and the
CSF backend for v10+, but nothing for v9, which has Valhall descriptors and
a Job Manager. This adds v9 to the JM backend:

- compute: v9 COMPUTE_JOB payload (shader environment with resource table,
  FAU, SPD and TLS) for dispatches and the precompiled helper kernels;
- draws: one MALLOC_VERTEX job per draw and layer, with the Valhall
  descriptors (resource tables, blend and depth/stencil descriptors) that the
  CSF backend passes through registers packed into the job;
- indexed draws are direct; indirect draws are patched on the GPU by a new
  libpan kernel (panlib_patch_malloc_vertex_job);
- layers and multiview are emulated with one draw per layer, as on Bifrost;
- the GPU writes the vertex packet pointer into the DCD of MALLOC_VERTEX
  jobs, so that is reset before a batch is issued again;
- LD_TILE cannot wait on the resource before v10, and storing to
  multisampled images from compute gives wrong results on v9, so
  multisampled copies use the graphics path.

v9 is gated behind PAN_I_WANT_A_BROKEN_VULKAN_DRIVER=1 like other
not-well-tested architectures and reports Vulkan 1.0.

Tested on a Pixel 6 (Mali-G78 MP20, panfrost DRM): VK-GL-CTS 1.4.4, every
5th test of the default mustpass: 126127 pass, failures only in tests that
are flaky or failing upstream on other Mali GPUs or that check for
conformance; vkcube, vkmark and the GTK4 Vulkan renderer.

The community v9 PanVK port for Mali-G57 on kbase
(https://github.com/Lock283/panvk-g99-jm) showed which pieces were
missing; no code from it is included.

